<doc>Pre-processing rules applied before parsing to keep payload deterministic and avoid parser pollution.</doc>
INSTRUCTION HYGIENE:

Remove all <doc>…</doc> blocks from input payload before parsing (byte-stream safe).
Remove all empty strings ("") within CONFIGURATION section before parsing.

<doc>Here you define how post-its should be treated when extracted. So any change regarding that should (if possible) always placed here instead of at module level.</doc>
For all post-it extractions:
    Only extract text from actual handwritten square post-its.
    Post-its are square with a general standard size of 3x3 inches.
    All post-its are handwritten.
    Detect every individual post-it in the read area and extract each one separately.
    If multiple post-its are present in one read area, process them in top-to-bottom, then left-to-right order.
    Only extract text written inside the borders of the post-it.
    Ignore any printed board text, template text, headings, labels, legends, axis text, rating-scale text, octagon text, connector lines, or any other non-post-it content, even if it appears inside, near, or overlapping the read area.
    The read area defines where to search for post-its, not which non-post-it text to extract.
    Preserve the original wording of each post-it.
    Apply only light normalization: correct obvious typos, normalize case, and remove line-break hyphenation.
    Do not summarize, reinterpret, merge, or paraphrase.
    If text is only partially legible, extract all legible text line by line and leave uncertain or incomplete text unresolved rather than guessing.
    If a post-it is only partially legible, perform a second pass on a tighter crop of that individual post-it before final extraction.
    If any extracted post-it text appears truncated, incomplete, or low-confidence, re-inspect that exact post-it in a tighter crop before returning the final result.
    Only keep text incomplete if the second pass still does not make the missing part legible.

<doc>Here you place document/picture normalization instructions, in case documents/pictures are not provided in normal reading direction.</doc>
For all OCR and visual extraction tasks:
    First normalize the orientation of the source so text is upright in normal reading direction.
    If needed, rotate the page or picture before OCR.
    Perform all spatial interpretations (top, bottom, left, right, rows, columns, quadrants) only after orientation normalization.

<doc>Here you define the coordination system, if it is necessary to precisely instruct the OCR actions.</doc>
Coordinate system:
    x increases from left to right
    y increases from top to bottom (y = 0% is top of page)


TOOLS:
<doc>This is a method to generate unique IDs for objects in a consistent and deterministic way.</doc>
{METHOD_ID_GENERATOR}({namespace}, {input}):
    Normalize: trim whitespace, lowercase, apply Unicode NFC.
    Concatenate namespace and string as "{namespace}|{input}".
    Hash with SHA‑256.
    Take the first 8 bytes as a big‑endian unsigned integer.
    Compute modulo 10^12, zero‑pad to 12 digits.
    Namespace: {namespace}
    Input: {input}
    Checksum: none (use all 12 digits for data).
    Output format: return 12-digit string.


<doc>Use this section to define the main configurations and also the metrics for the files where the information should be extracted from.</doc>
CONFIGURATION:

{JSON_SCHEMA} = "ws_classes.schema.json" <doc>we are still using the JSON schema as reference for the structure to use.</doc>
<doc>Global runtime constants used for extraction and ID generation across all modules.</doc>
{CUSTOMER_NAME} = "WEIG"
{TARGET_FILE} = lower({CUSTOMER_NAME}) + „_ws_results.json“
{COMMON_ABBREVIATIONS} = "KI, HCM, SAP"
{ABBREVIATION_CORRECTIONS} = "HCL->HCM, S.A.P->SAP, K.I->KI"

{WORKSHOP_DATE} = "2026-04-14"
{NOTE_COUNTER} = 0

<doc>Here you define the file name where the Free Association module has been digitized and from where the post-its should be read-out.</doc>
{MD_FREE_ASSOCIATION_FILE} = "weig_FreeAssociation.pdf"
{MD_FREE_ASSOCIATION_READ_AREA} = All post-its that can be identified.

<doc>Here you define the file name where the Value Effort Matrix module has been digitized and from which areas the post-its should be read-out in the different context.</doc>
{MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_FILE} = "weig_ValueEffortMatrix.pdf"
{MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA} = All post-its sticking in rectangle area with color of {TARGET_FILE}.container_ValueEffortMatrix.module_ValueEffortMatrix.teamName

<doc>Here you define the file name where the Detailed Idea plus Investment module has been digitized and from which areas the post-its should be read-out in the different context.</doc>
{MD_DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT_FILE} = "weig_DetailedIdeaInvestment.pdf"

<doc>Here you define the file name where the Roadmap module has been digitized and from which areas the post-its should be read-out.</doc>
{MD_USER_JOURNEY_FILE} = "weig_Roadmap.pdf"
{MD_USER_JOURNEY_READ_AREA} = Rectangle area within {MD_USER_JOURNEY_FILE} with a picture as background.
{MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H3_01} = Upper left quadrant of {MD_USER_JOURNEY_READ_AREA}
{MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H3_02} = Upper center quadrant of {MD_USER_JOURNEY_READ_AREA}
{MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H3_03} = Upper right quadrant of {MD_USER_JOURNEY_READ_AREA}
{MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H2_01} = Middle left quadrant of {MD_USER_JOURNEY_READ_AREA}
{MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H2_02} = Middle center quadrant of {MD_USER_JOURNEY_READ_AREA}
{MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H2_03} = Middle right quadrant of {MD_USER_JOURNEY_READ_AREA}
{MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H1_01} = Lower left quadrant of {MD_USER_JOURNEY_READ_AREA}
{MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H1_02} = Lower center quadrant of {MD_USER_JOURNEY_READ_AREA}
{MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H1_03} = Lower right quadrant of {MD_USER_JOURNEY_READ_AREA}

<doc>Here you only update the already exting {TARGET_FILE} that has been created in the 'prefill' step. We use the properties of {TARGET_FILE} directly to clearly instruct the LLM for mapping.</doc>
EXECUTION:

Structure for the data mapping = {JSON_SCHEMA}:

<doc>Populate Free Association by reading all post-its in the configured area and appending as PostIt notes.</doc>
Update {TARGET_FILE}.module_FreeAssociation.freeAssociation
    
    Extract text from each post-it in {MD_FREE_ASSOCIATION_READ_AREA} from {MD_FREE_ASSOCIATION_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.

    For each post-it extracted:
        {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
        PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
            PostIt.note = text extracted from the post-it
            append PostIt to {TARGET_FILE}.module_FreeAssociation.freeAssociation  


<doc>Populate Value/Effort modules per team and classify each extracted idea into a weight category based on location.</doc>
Update {TARGET_FILE}.container_ValueEffortMatrix.module_ValueEffortMatrix
    
    For each teamName:
        Extract text from each post-it in {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA} from {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.

        For each post-it extracted:
            Create WorkshopItemWeighted with:
                id = "ITEM_" + {METHOD_ID_GENERATOR}({CUSTOMER_NAME}, teamName + {NOTE_COUNTER})
                
                {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                PostIt.note = text extracted from the post-it
                idea = PostIt

                If post-it is located in upper left quadrant of {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA} next to a drawing of a head with a lightbulb:
                    category = Big Bet
                Else if post-it is located in upper right quadrant of {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA}:
                    category = Quick Win
                Else if post-it is located in left half or lower third of {MD_VALUE_EFFORT_MATRIX_READ_AREA}:
                    category = Nice to have
                Else:
                    category = Wise Choice

            append WorkshopItemWeighted to Module_ValueEffortMatrix.workshopItemWeighted           
      

<doc>Populate Detailed Idea Investment per team.</doc>
Update {TARGET_FILE}.container_DetailedIdeaInvestment.module_DetailedIdeaInvestment
    
    For each teamName:
        
        {MD_DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT_READ_AREA} = All post-its in rectangle area WHERE background cólor corresponds to teamName.
        {IDEA_COUNTER} = 0
        
        For each detailedIdea:
            {IDEA_COUNTER} = {IDEA_COUNTER} + 1
            {DETAILED_IDEA_FIRST_ROW} = Extract text from each post-it in row {IDEA_COUNTER} of {MD_DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT_READ_AREA} from {MD_DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.
            {IDEA_COUNTER} = {IDEA_COUNTER} + 1
            {DETAILED_IDEA_SECOND_ROW} = Extract text from each post-it in row {IDEA_COUNTER} of {MD_DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT_READ_AREA} from {MD_DETAILED_IDEA_INVESTMENT_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.
            {DETAILED_IDEA_COMPLETE} = {DETAILED_IDEA_FIRST_ROW} + {DETAILED_IDEA_SECOND_ROW}

            i = 0
            For each detailedIdeaStep in detailedIdea:
                i = i + 1
                {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                PostIt.note = text extracted from post-it(i) in {DETAILED_IDEA_COMPLETE}
                note = PostIt

                append note to detailedIdeaStep.note


<doc>Populate Roadmap module.</doc>
Update {TARGET_FILE}.module_Roadmap
    
    For each {MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H1_XX}:
        Extract text from each post-it in {MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H1_XX} from {MD_USER_JOURNEY_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.

        For each post-it extracted:
            Create roadmapItem with:
                {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                PostIt.note = text extracted from the post-it
                idea = PostIt
                category = H1
                wave = XX
                id = "ROADMAP_ITEM_" + {METHOD_ID_GENERATOR}({CUSTOMER_NAME}, "RoadmapItem" + {NOTE_COUNTER})
                
            append RoadmapItem to Module_Roadmap.roadmapItem

    For each {MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H2_XX}:
        Extract text from each post-it in {MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H2_XX} from {MD_USER_JOURNEY_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.

        For each post-it extracted:
            Create roadmapItem with:
                {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                PostIt.note = text extracted from the post-it
                idea = PostIt
                category = H2
                wave = XX
                id = "ROADMAP_ITEM_" + {METHOD_ID_GENERATOR}({CUSTOMER_NAME}, "RoadmapItem" + {NOTE_COUNTER})
                
            append RoadmapItem to Module_Roadmap.roadmapItem

    For each {MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H3_XX}:
        Extract text from each post-it in {MD_USER_JOURNEY_QUADRANT_H3_XX} from {MD_USER_JOURNEY_FILE} using OCR and light normalization.

        For each post-it extracted:
            Create roadmapItem with:
                {NOTE_COUNTER} = {NOTE_COUNTER} + 1
                PostIt.id = {NOTE_COUNTER}
                PostIt.note = text extracted from the post-it
                idea = PostIt
                category = H3
                wave = XX
                id = "ROADMAP_ITEM_" + {METHOD_ID_GENERATOR}({CUSTOMER_NAME}, "RoadmapItem" + {NOTE_COUNTER})
                
            append RoadmapItem to Module_Roadmap.roadmapItem    
